@startuml sequence-diagram-2

' Sheet 2/4 - A4 portrait. See sequence-diagram.puml for the whole diagram.
skinparam dpi 200
scale max 1500*2150

title node-sso-consumer - WSS authentication and realtime delivery of ME\nSheet 2/4: WebSocket Secure and double authentication

autonumber 26

actor "User" as User

participant "Front Application\nBrowser" as Browser
participant "SSO Client\nnode-sso-consumer/client" as Client
participant "Node Application\nnode-sso-consumer" as App
participant "Realtime Bridge\nnode-sso-consumer" as Bridge
participant "x-core\nSSO / Realtime Provider" as XCore


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED FROM SHEET 1/4:
the client holds a short-lived, single-use ticket.
end note


== 4. Opening the WebSocket Secure ==

Client -> Bridge : WSS /_ws/realtime?ticket=XXXXX

note over Client, Bridge
WSS = WebSocket Secure

Persistent connection
encrypted by TLS.
end note

alt No ticket in the URL
    Bridge --> Client : HTTP 401
    note right of Bridge
    Refused BEFORE the upgrade:
    the socket never exists.
    end note
else Ticket present
    Bridge -> Bridge : Redeems the ticket\nread AND remove, in one move
    Bridge -> Bridge : ticket -> accessToken
end

alt Ticket invalid / expired / already spent
    Bridge --> Client : close 4402
    note right of Client
    4402 is NOT a session that is over.

    The client asks for another ticket
    and dials again at once, with no backoff.
    end note
else Ticket valid

    == 5. Authenticating the APPLICATION against x-core ==

    Bridge -> XCore : Opens the Realtime WSS\nHMAC-signed handshake

    note over Bridge, XCore
    HMAC answers:

    "WHICH APPLICATION
    is opening this connection?"
    end note

    XCore -> XCore : HMAC signature verification

    XCore --> Bridge : WebSocket accepted


    == 6. Authenticating the USER ==

    Bridge -> XCore : AUTH frame\n{ accessToken }

    note over Bridge, XCore
    accessToken answers:

    "WHICH USER
    is behind this connection?"

    Expected within seconds of the socket
    opening, or x-core closes with 4002.
    end note

    XCore -> XCore : accessToken verification
    XCore -> XCore : User identification

    XCore --> Bridge : User auth OK


    note over Client, XCore
    The browser never sends
    the AUTH frame itself.

    The Bridge sends it on its behalf.

    An AUTH frame coming from
    the browser is refused.
    end note


    == 7. Subscribing to the realtime ME ==

    Client -> Bridge : WebSocket frame\nsubscribe { topic: "me-changed" }

    Bridge -> XCore : WebSocket frame\nsubscribe { topic: "me-changed" }

    Client -> Bridge : subscribe { topic: "me-signed-out" }

    Bridge -> XCore : subscribe { topic: "me-signed-out" }

    Client -> Bridge : subscribe { topic: "me-sessions" }

    Bridge -> XCore : subscribe { topic: "me-sessions" }

    note over Client, Bridge
    The browser subscribes the instant ITS socket opens,
    which is BEFORE the one to x-core is up.

    The Bridge queues these frames
    and replays them on "open" rather than dropping them.
    end note

    note over Client, XCore
    From here on:

    the connection stays OPEN.

    No polling.
    No GET /me every X seconds.
    end note

end


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED ON SHEET 3/4, inside the "Ticket valid" branch:
standing by and receiving the ME over WebSocket.
end note

@enduml
